.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.TH CLEVOCTL 1 "" "clevo-control @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clevoctl \- keyboard backlight and performance profile of Clevo laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clevoctl status
.br
.B clevoctl backlight color
.I COLOR
.br
.B clevoctl backlight brightness
.I LEVEL
.br
.B clevoctl backlight
.RB { on | off | save | restore }
.br
.B clevoctl profile
.RB { list | get }
.br
.B clevoctl profile set
.I PROFILE
.br
.B clevoctl \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clevoctl
controls the devices exposed by the
.B clevo\-control
kernel module: the RGB keyboard backlight and the firmware performance
profile. Members of the
.B plugdev
group can use it without root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the backlight color, the brightness, the color saved for the next boot
and the active performance profile. A device that does not exist is shown as
.BR "not available" .
.SS Backlight
.TP
.BI "backlight color " COLOR
Set the color and remember it.
.I COLOR
is
.BR #RRGGBB ,
.BR RRGGBB ,
.B #RGB
or one of the names
.BR white ,
.BR red ,
.BR orange ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR green ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR blue ,
.BR purple ,
.BR pink ,
.BR magenta .
.TP
.BI "backlight brightness " LEVEL
Set the brightness.
.I LEVEL
is an integer from 0 to the maximum shown by
.BR status ,
or a percentage from
.B 0%
to
.BR 100% .
.TP
.B backlight on
Turn the backlight on at half brightness if it is off.
.TP
.B backlight off
Turn the backlight off (brightness 0).
.TP
.B backlight save
Remember the color shown now, for example one chosen with the Fn color key.
Run when
.B clevo\-control\-backlight.service
stops.
.TP
.B backlight restore
Apply the remembered color. Run when
.B clevo\-control\-backlight.service
starts. Nothing remembered is not an error.
.SS Performance profile
.TP
.B profile list
List the available profiles, the active one marked with an asterisk.
.TP
.B profile get
Print the active profile.
.TP
.BI "profile set " PROFILE
Select a profile:
.BR quiet ,
.BR low\-power ,
.B balanced
or
.BR performance .
See
.BR clevo\-control (7)
for how this interacts with the desktop power mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A device is missing, access was denied, a value is invalid, or an I/O error
occurred. One line is printed to standard error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/clevo\-control/backlight\-color
The remembered color: six hexadecimal digits.
.TP
.I /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight/
The keyboard backlight.
.TP
.I /sys/class/platform\-profile/
The platform profile handler named
.BR clevo .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
For testing, and for a backlight with another name:
.TP
.B CLEVO_CONTROL_LED
LED directory used instead of
.IR /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight .
.TP
.B CLEVO_CONTROL_PROFILE_CLASS
Directory used instead of
.IR /sys/class/platform\-profile .
.TP
.B CLEVO_CONTROL_STATE
File used instead of
.IR /var/lib/clevo\-control/backlight\-color .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
clevoctl backlight color '#ff00ff'
clevoctl backlight color orange
clevoctl backlight brightness 50%
clevoctl profile set quiet
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clevo\-control (7),
.BR clevo\-control\-tray (1),
.BR powerprofilesctl (1)
